### Inheritance in Java

**Definition:** Inheritance is an OOP concept where a **child class (subclass)** acquires the properties and methods of a **parent class (superclass)** using the `extends` keyword.

**Purpose:** Code reuse, method overriding, is-a relationship.

**Types:**
- Single, Multilevel, Hierarchical (Java supports these)
- Multiple inheritance NOT supported through classes (use interfaces)

**Example:**
```java
class Animal {
    void eat() { System.out.println("Animal eats"); }
}

class Dog extends Animal {   // Dog inherits Animal
    void bark() { System.out.println("Dog barks"); }
}

Dog d = new Dog();
d.eat();   // inherited from Animal
d.bark();  // own method
```

