### Java Program Demonstrating "this" and "super" Keywords

- **`this` Keyword**: Refers to the current class instance variable, method, or invokes another constructor within the same class (`this()`).
- **`super` Keyword**: Refers to the immediate parent class instance variable, overridden method, or invokes the superclass constructor (`super()`).

```java
// Parent Class
class Person {
    String name;
    int age;

    // Superclass constructor
    Person(String name, int age) {
        this.name = name;
        this.age = age;
    }

    void display() {
        System.out.println("Name: " + name + ", Age: " + age);
    }
}

// Subclass
class Student extends Person {
    int rollNo;
    String course;

    Student(String name, int age, int rollNo, String course) {
        super(name, age);      // 1. Invoking parent class constructor
        this.rollNo = rollNo;  // 2. 'this' resolves variable shadowing
        this.course = course;
    }

    @Override
    void display() {
        super.display();       // 3. Invoking parent class method
        System.out.println("Roll No: " + this.rollNo + ", Course: " + this.course);
        System.out.println("Accessing parent name via super: " + super.name);
    }
}

public class ThisSuperDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Student s = new Student("Amaan", 20, 101, "Computer Science");
        s.display();
    }
}
```

**Output:**
```text
Name: Amaan, Age: 20
Roll No: 101, Course: Computer Science
Accessing parent name via super: Amaan
```

