### Class and Constructor Overloading

#### Class Definition:
A **class** is a **blueprint/template** for creating objects. It defines:
- **Fields** (data members) – represent the state
- **Methods** – represent the behavior
- **Constructors** – initialize the object

```java
class ClassName {
    // Fields
    dataType fieldName;

    // Constructor
    ClassName(parameters) { }

    // Methods
    returnType methodName(parameters) { }
}
```

---

#### Constructor Overloading:
Defining **multiple constructors** in the same class with different parameter lists.

**Example – `Student` class with overloaded constructors:**
```java
class Student {
    String name;
    int rollNo;
    double marks;
    String branch;

    // Constructor 1: Default
    Student() {
        name   = "Unknown";
        rollNo = 0;
        marks  = 0.0;
        branch = "CSE";
    }

    // Constructor 2: Name and Roll only
    Student(String name, int rollNo) {
        this.name   = name;
        this.rollNo = rollNo;
        this.marks  = 0.0;
        this.branch = "CSE";
    }

    // Constructor 3: All fields
    Student(String name, int rollNo, double marks, String branch) {
        this.name   = name;
        this.rollNo = rollNo;
        this.marks  = marks;
        this.branch = branch;
    }

    void display() {
        System.out.println("Roll: " + rollNo + " | Name: " + name
                           + " | Branch: " + branch + " | Marks: " + marks);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Student s1 = new Student();                              // Constructor 1
        Student s2 = new Student("Ravi", 101);                   // Constructor 2
        Student s3 = new Student("Priya", 102, 92.5, "ECE");     // Constructor 3

        s1.display();
        s2.display();
        s3.display();
    }
}
```

**Output:**
```
Roll: 0  | Name: Unknown | Branch: CSE | Marks: 0.0
Roll: 101 | Name: Ravi   | Branch: CSE | Marks: 0.0
Roll: 102 | Name: Priya  | Branch: ECE | Marks: 92.5
```

