### Constructor Definition and Types in Java

- **Definition**: A **constructor** is a special member method having the exact same name as its class and no explicit return type (not even `void`). It is invoked automatically when an object is instantiated using the `new` operator.

#### Types of Constructors:
1. **Default (No-Argument) Constructor**: Either generated by the compiler or explicitly written to provide default member values.
2. **Parameterized Constructor**: Accepts arguments to initialize specific values for each object instance.
3. **Copy Constructor**: Initializes an object using another object of the same class.

```java
class Student {
    String name;
    int rollNo;

    // 1. Default constructor
    Student() {
        this.name = "Unknown";
        this.rollNo = 0;
    }

    // 2. Parameterized constructor
    Student(String name, int rollNo) {
        this.name = name;
        this.rollNo = rollNo;
    }

    // 3. Copy constructor
    Student(Student s) {
        this.name = s.name;
        this.rollNo = s.rollNo;
    }
}
```

