solutions.oopj|what is polymorphism explain runtim:
### Polymorphism and Runtime Polymorphism in Detail

**Polymorphism** (from Greek *poly* = many, *morph* = forms) is the OOP concept allowing a single message or method invocation to behave differently depending on the invoking object.

#### Runtime Polymorphism (Dynamic Method Dispatch)
- Runtime polymorphism is resolved at runtime through **method overriding**.
- When an overridden method is called through a superclass reference variable, Java determines which version of the method to execute based upon the **actual object type being referred to**, not the reference variable's type.

```java
// Base class
class Animal {
    void makeSound() {
        System.out.println("Animal makes a sound");
    }
}

// Subclasses overriding makeSound()
class Dog extends Animal {
    @Override
    void makeSound() {
        System.out.println("Dog barks: Woof Woof");
    }
}

class Cat extends Animal {
    @Override
    void makeSound() {
        System.out.println("Cat meows: Meow Meow");
    }
}

public class DynamicDispatchDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Animal ref; // Superclass reference

        ref = new Dog();
        ref.makeSound(); // Prints: Dog barks: Woof Woof

        ref = new Cat();
        ref.makeSound(); // Prints: Cat meows: Meow Meow
    }
}
```

