### Variables in an Interface in Java

In a Java interface, all member variables are implicitly:
**`public static final`**

1. **`public`**: Accessible by any class implementing or referring to the interface.
2. **`static`**: Associated with the interface itself, not with any implementing class instance. Accessed as `InterfaceName.VARIABLE_NAME`.
3. **`final`**: Acts as a constant. Its value cannot be modified after declaration; it must be initialized at declaration time.

```java
interface Config {
    int MAX_CONNECTIONS = 100; // Implicitly public static final
}

public class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(Config.MAX_CONNECTIONS);
        // Config.MAX_CONNECTIONS = 200; // Compiler Error! Cannot assign a value to final variable
    }
}
```

