### Java Program: Multiple Interfaces for Calculating Area and Volume

```java
// Interface for 2D Area
interface AreaCalculable {
    double calculateArea();
}

// Interface for 3D Volume
interface VolumeCalculable {
    double calculateVolume();
}

// Cylinder implements both 2D and 3D interfaces
class Cylinder implements AreaCalculable, VolumeCalculable {
    double radius;
    double height;

    Cylinder(double radius, double height) {
        this.radius = radius;
        this.height = height;
    }

    @Override
    public double calculateArea() {
        // Total surface area: 2*pi*r*h + 2*pi*r^2
        return 2 * Math.PI * radius * height + 2 * Math.PI * radius * radius;
    }

    @Override
    public double calculateVolume() {
        // Volume: pi*r^2*h
        return Math.PI * radius * radius * height;
    }
}

public class MultiInterfaceDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Cylinder cyl = new Cylinder(5.0, 10.0);
        System.out.printf("Cylinder Surface Area: %.2f%n", cyl.calculateArea());
        System.out.printf("Cylinder Volume       : %.2f%n", cyl.calculateVolume());
    }
}
```

