### Differences Between Method Overloading and Overriding with Examples

- **Overloading**: Same class, same method name, different parameter lists (compile-time).
  ```java
  int sum(int a, int b) { return a + b; }
  double sum(double a, double b) { return a + b; }
  ```
- **Overriding**: Subclass redefines parent method with exact same signature (runtime).
  ```java
  class Parent { void greet() { System.out.println("Hello Parent"); } }
  class Child extends Parent { void greet() { System.out.println("Hello Child"); } }
  ```

