### Suspending and Resuming Threads in Java

In modern Java, legacy methods `suspend()` and `resume()` are deprecated due to deadlock hazards. Suspending and resuming is implemented safely using **flags and `wait()` / `notify()`**:

```java
class SuspendableThread implements Runnable {
    private boolean suspended = false;

    public void run() {
        try {
            for (int i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {
                System.out.println("Step " + i);
                synchronized (this) {
                    while (suspended) {
                        wait();
                    }
                }
                Thread.sleep(500);
            }
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {}
    }

    public synchronized void suspendThread() { suspended = true; }
    public synchronized void resumeThread() { suspended = false; notify(); }
}
```

